    "Deliberate repetition for emphasis or rhythm: never suggest a synonym to 'avoid repeating' a word; elegant variation is the machine habit.",
    "Regional and variant spellings (colour/color, organise/organize, grey/gray, programme/program; Danish variant spellings such as resurse/ressource, majonæse/mayonnaise): detect the document's variety and follow it; never flip.",
    "Profanity and strong language: never soften, mask, asterisk or replace.",
    "Dialect, slang, code-switching and loanwords (Scots, AAVE, Hiberno-English, Jutlandic forms, 'det er nice', 'vi skal deploye'): not errors.",
    "Hedges the writer chose (I think, probably, as far as I can tell, jeg tror, måske): never delete to make text sound more confident.",
    "First person and direct address (I, we, you, jeg, vi, du): never passivise or shift to third person.",
    "Sentence-initial And, But, So, Because, Og, Men: never flag.",
    "Short, one-sentence and uneven paragraphs: never merge or pad.",
    "The writer's punctuation habits (em dashes, spaced en dashes, semicolons, Oxford comma, exclamation marks, ellipses, straight vs curly quotes): match the document, never mass-convert.",
    "Deliberate lowercase, brand casing, and ALL CAPS for a shouted word: never recase.",
    "Absence of headings, bullets or bold: not a defect; never add structure.",
    "Numbers as written (three vs 3, 40% vs forty percent): never normalise.",
    "Anything inside quotation marks, code spans, code blocks, URLs, or citations: never touch.",
    "Rhetorical questions, asides in parentheses, jokes and personal anecdotes: never remove or neutralise.",
    "A word the writer has already typed most of: may be completed even if it is on the never_suggest list, but never ranked above a plain alternative and never proposed unprompted."
  ]
}
